From fc439857a7fbef5cfb6749056640ee219b805d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] GDN: read the KDA state from the cache by ids, Vulkan
 writes snapshots back in place

- ggml_gated_delta_net_ids(q, k, v, g, beta, states, ids, K): the initial
  state of seq s is row ids[s] of states (src[6]). CPU reference; Vulkan binds
  ids; every other backend reports it unsupported in supports_op.
- glm5-next KDA (rollback snapshots on, one seq, one cell, no state to clear):
  read the SSM state straight from its cache row through s_copy instead of the
  4 MiB build_rs gather per layer, if the layer's device supports the op.
- Vulkan: fuse GATED_DELTA_NET -> views -> CPY of its snapshots into the
  recurrent cache (GDN_CACHE): the shader writes the snapshots to the cache
  rows directly (per-seq and per-slot strides from the CPY view) and the CPY is
  skipped (port of the CUDA/SYCL fusion; upstream draft #27973 bound the wrong
  buffer and ignored the slot stride, so this is a rewrite). Every invocation
  reads its state shard before writing any snapshot, so the snapshot rows may
  alias the rows read through ids; with ids, the fusion requires n_seqs == 1.
  graph_optimize keeps GDN + views + CPY adjacent.
- test-backend-ops: GATED_DELTA_NET_IDS_CACHE (glm5-next cache layout with K
  rollback planes, ids into each plane, in-place snapshot write; n 1-5, K 1/3,
  1-2 seqs, H 64 S 128).

Upstream #30139 (read recurrent states in place) does nothing for this config:
it turns itself off when rollback snapshots are kept (n_rs_seq > 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
